' ============================================================ Notes
note as N_Verify
    **EndpointSpec / OperationSpec.verify** (Information Expert, SPEC-V01 … V17)

    ""EndpointSpec.verify(call):""
    ""  if isEmpty(): return Verdict.notVerified(false)""
    ""  if isPreflight(call): return Verdict.notVerified(true)""
    ""  op = operations.get(method of call)""
    ""  if op == null: return Verdict with UNSPECIFIED_METHOD""
    ""  return op.verify(call)""
    ""OperationSpec.verify(call):""
    ""  content type check if contentTypes not empty""
    ""  malformed body -> MALFORMED_BODY, skip body checks""
    ""  for a in call.getArguments():""
    ""    p = find(a)  // location + name, most specific""
    ""    if p != null: checks.add(p.check(a))""
    ""    else if declares(a.location) and not header: EXTRA_ARGUMENT""
    ""    else: unchecked.add(a)""
    ""  for each required p without argument: MISSING_ARGUMENT""
    ""  warnings: request warnings + type warnings + repeated names""
    ""  return new Verdict(checks, violations, unchecked, warnings)""
end note

note as N_Types
    **ParameterType** (Polymorphism, like ""PathSegment"")
    Each subclass owns its grammar (SPEC-T03 … T07); ""check"" never trims
    and knows text values vs JSON kinds. Integer and Decimal hold an
    optional range and add the PRECISION warning (SPEC-T11).
end note

note as N_Cache
    **Endpoint** (Creator of ""RecordedCall"", Expert for its spec)

    ""record(call, path):""
    ""  if not pattern.matches(path): return false""
    ""  parsed = RequestParser.parse(call.getRequest(), pattern.argumentsOf(path))""
    ""  calls.add(new RecordedCall(call, parsed))""
    ""addSpecItem(item):  spec = spec.with(item); verdicts.clear()""
    ""createReport():""
    ""  s = spec   // read once, one spec per report (SPEC-L02)""
    ""  for c in copy of calls: verdicts c -> verdictOf(c, s)""
    ""  return new EndpointReport(..., s, verdicts)""
end note

note as N_Parse
    **RequestParser** and **JsonReader** (Pure Fabrication, like ""UrlPath"")
    Hand-written scanners, no regular expressions (SPEC-L04).
    Path arguments come from ""EndpointPattern"" (US10), then query
    (SPEC-Q), body (JSON SPEC-J or form SPEC-Q), headers (SPEC-H).
    Limits: 200 arguments, depth 10 (SPEC-L01). Never throws.
end note

note as N_Fields
    **FieldName** (Pure Fabrication): parts split on ""."", each
    ""key"" + any ""[]"" / ""{}"" (SPEC-J09). ""matches"" walks the parts;
    ""{}"" matches any one key (SPEC-J10); ""isMoreSpecificThan""
    prefers a concrete key at the leftmost difference (SPEC-J11).
end note

note as N_Legend
    **Legend**: green = new in US11; yellow ""<<changed>>"" = US10 class,
    only new or changed members shown; white without members =
    unchanged US10 class (see US10 class diagram v3).
end note

